# Native EMA study analysis and publication handoff

**Disclosure.** This report was machine-generated with OpenAI Codex. The study adapts SakanaAI/AI-Scientist's pinned 2D diffusion template. Its measurements come from retained local MPS executions. The critique below is provisional and from the same model family; neither it nor the deterministic checks constitutes independent scientific peer review.

All four authorized operations completed successfully in the requested order. This session made no manual changes to scientific source, frozen material, protocol, resource ceilings, raw data, or claims. The publication worker performed the authorized disclosure and link transformation. This session launched no agents or additional native sessions, changed no model defaults, and performed no commit or push. Figure inspection and repository delivery remain the coordinator's responsibility.

The study-local analysis, writing, and audit wrappers, `ALLAGMA.md`, `DESIGN.md`, `protocol.json`, and `DISCLOSURE.md` were read. Campaign `ema-v1` resolved all three methods to bundle `b-2b63431e34a085598aaade78`, lock ID `7287e278da3e264dc83704d42c334dd5845da048f59c9967343545fc4ec6c329`. Its catalog and the exact canonical `SKILL.md` and adjacent `module.yaml` for each method were read. Each following entry command returned exit code 0 with the campaign-pinned method path:

```sh
python3 .allagma/bundles/b-2b63431e34a085598aaade78/tools/allagma.py entry --study . --campaign ema-v1 --module research/analysis
python3 .allagma/bundles/b-2b63431e34a085598aaade78/tools/allagma.py entry --study . --campaign ema-v1 --module research/writing
python3 .allagma/bundles/b-2b63431e34a085598aaade78/tools/allagma.py entry --study . --campaign ema-v1 --module research/audit
```

Read-only artifact inspection verified the freeze's protocol and campaign-lock digests, all 11 frozen code/material digests, four orchestration digests, and four successful pilot-record digests. The freeze was recorded at `2026-10-07T15:28:26.950456+00:00`; every confirmation attempt started later. Exactly the ten planned confirmation trajectories succeeded: moons seeds 1001–1005 and mixture seeds 2001–2005. All 15 attempt records remain retained: ten confirmation successes, four pilot successes, and the deliberately interrupted `pilot-moons-11-a001`. The [raw manifest](../../campaigns/ema-v1/analyses/a001/raw-manifest.json) includes exactly ten confirmation raw inputs and explicitly excludes all five pilot attempts, identifying the interrupted attempt by status. The analysis is marked `partial: false`.

| Command, in execution order | Exit | Charged seconds | Supervisor receipt |
| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |
| `python3 manage.py analyze` | 0 | 15.517920332960784 | [019-analyze.json](../compute/019-analyze.json) |
| `python3 manage.py audit` | 0 | 4.819993916898966 | [020-audit.json](../compute/020-audit.json) |
| `python3 manage.py verify` | 0 | 6.804718292085454 | [021-independent-verification.json](../compute/021-independent-verification.json) |
| `python3 publication.py` | 0 | 0.04027158301323652 | [022-publication.json](../compute/022-publication.json) |

The first three operations reserved 122 seconds each, with 120-second process limits; publication reserved 17 seconds with a 15-second limit. Each normally completed operation was charged its actual elapsed time. Running commands were awaited until completion. No operation failed or was refused for budget.

The [deterministic audit](../../campaigns/ema-v1/latest-audit.json) passed with 305 checked references, no stale claims, and no findings. It repeated the frozen analysis once in a separate output directory, compared output digests, and regenerated the manuscript and claims. The [separate verifier](../independent-verification.json) passed 263 distinct direct-reference checks, 84 SciPy projected-W1 comparisons, 84 saved-weight digests, 42 mixture-coverage checks, and eight primary paired-interval comparisons, including primary differences and sign-flip sensitivity. Counts include the four pilot successes for verification only; pilots remain excluded from confirmation inference. It regenerated all three weight variants at both checkpoints for confirmation seeds 1001 and 2001: all 12 sample arrays had maximum absolute error `0.0`. This reused frozen model/sampling code and did not retrain.

The [published manuscript](../../publication/manuscript.md) places its machine-generation disclosure immediately after the title. The [publication receipt](../../publication/record.json) records the original manuscript, published manuscript, transformation script, disclosure, analysis, and claims by digest. Its worker repeated the text transformation and verified local link targets. The scientific wording and numbers were preserved. The published manuscript SHA-256 is `0b69adf92abaccf8027a512be8afc84bd6226bcd3a121212166010e419af4a4a`.

The published manuscript, all eight [claim records](../../campaigns/ema-v1/analyses/a001/paper/claims.json), the complete [numerical summary](../../campaigns/ema-v1/analyses/a001/outputs/summary.json), and per-seed metrics were read. No discrepancy was found among the primary reported means, intervals, improved-seed counts, sign-flip values, or abstract totals. All four 5,000-update mean differences favor EMA. Across both checkpoints, six of eight means favor EMA and three unadjusted t intervals lie entirely below zero. All four 10,000-update intervals contain zero; the two mixture means at that checkpoint slightly favor raw weights. All confirmation mixture variants cover all eight modes, so their observed coverage differences and estimated standard errors are zero. This saturation does not establish population equivalence. Every sign-flip p-value is at least 0.0625. The comparisons remain descriptive, with five seeds per dataset and no familywise superiority conclusion.

The following reporting issues remain for coordinator inspection; no frozen output was changed to address them:

1. The verifier receipt's statement that all reported SW1 scores and paired confidence intervals were independently recomputed is broader than its implementation. The independent calculations cover model-versus-heldout SW1, primary paired intervals and sign-flip values, mixture counts/coverage/inlier fractions, and saved-weight/sample checks. The heldout-versus-heldout control distances, leave-one-out summaries, half-L1 diagnostic, and secondary mode/inlier intervals are reproduced by the frozen analyzer during audit, but are not independently recalculated by `verify_results.py`. Its pass should be interpreted with that narrower coverage.
2. Table 2's secondary numerical results agree with the summary, but the eight ClaimRecords cover only the primary SW1 comparisons. There are no distinct ClaimRecords for the secondary mode-coverage/inlier conclusions. This is a claim-ledger completeness gap, not a demonstrated numerical error.
3. The manuscript's reproducibility paragraph says the study README supplies metric/figure recomputation and training commands. At inspection, that README supplies environment setup and `manage.py status`, but not those commands. The manuscript also refers to a separate host report that is not linked or delivered in this package. These are documentation/delivery gaps for the coordinator, not evidence of a failed scientific run.

Bibliographic metadata was checked separately from empirical support. The titles, author lists, and years match the primary arXiv records for [Ho, Jain, and Abbeel (2020)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.11239) and [Nichol and Dhariwal (2021)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2102.09672). The cited [PyTorch 2.14 reproducibility page](https://docs.pytorch.org/docs/2.14/notes/randomness.html) resolves. The pinned GitHub directory and raw-file fetches returned browser-tool errors in this session; the pinned reference was inspected through retained provenance, attribution, and license files, without claiming a fresh remote-byte verification. Bibliographic checks do not validate this study's scientific conclusions.

After publication, the supervisor reports **276.34548083175906 seconds charged** and **1523.654519168241 seconds remaining** under the original **1800.0-second ceiling**. This includes the conservative 15.3-second prior estimate. There are **15 of 18 training attempts used**, leaving three attempt slots. Campaign phase is `audit`, execution status is `completed`, assurance is `deterministic`, and `next_run` is null. The [final status snapshot](final-status.json) and [command/material record](record.json) preserve this handoff state. No further scientific computation was run for this report.
